BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art as Self Discovery: Mixed Media Art  — Sebastopol Center For 
 the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261105T000000
DTEND:20261106T000000
UID:f56be7a5629329345a3d2f57b2067a3e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Art as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art (November 2026)\n\n  \n
     \n      \n        \n          $287.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nA
 rt as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art Every-Other Thursday\, 5:30-8:30pm\,
  November 5th\,  19th\, December 3rd\, and 17thAttendance: $275.00 + $12.0
 0 Materials Fee Class Description: In this 4 session series\, students wil
 l explore the art of creating mixed-media art with multiple techniques. Ma
 rion will guide you through the basics of composition\, color theory\, and
  image selection. This workshop is designed for people of all creative lev
 els who wish to learn collage and mixed media skills\, connect with the co
 mmunity\, and engage in meaningful self-expression. Students will have ac
 cess to a curated selection of collage materials\, paints\, and scissors\,
  and are encouraged to bring magazines and personal images of choice. We w
 ill explore image selection and composition\, layering and embedding 3D ob
 jects\, as well as choosing mounting surfaces and framing. Marion will off
 er individual and group guidance in each class. While we’ll appreciate 
 the aesthetic aspects of the work\, we will focus on the personal meaning 
 and process for each piece. This is a space for connection and non-judgeme
 nt\, where your unique creative expression matters above all - inviting cu
 riosity and play to reveal new pathways of seeing and creating. Students 
 are encouraged to bring the following materials: Gloves Preferred Glue 
 Preferred scissorsAbout the Teacher: Marion Ruta Segal has been a practici
 ng mixed media artist with nearly 20 years of teaching experience in New Y
 ork City and the San Francisco Bay Area. Her work has been exhibited publi
 cly since 2013. Marion has taught at community organizations and at the co
 llege level\, leading workshops that invite students into exploratory\, me
 aning-focused making - grounding them in core methods and aesthetics inclu
 ding design\, color theory\, and composition. She brings warmth\, depth\, 
 and care to the studio\, meeting participants wherever they are at creativ
 ely. Click here to learn more about Marion! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n           
