SUMMARY:Still Life in Acrylic  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Califo
 rnia
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261109T000000
UID:3f1934dea6a122dc35c90f821c0f108e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Still Life in Acrylic\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n         
  $67.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nStill Life in Acrylic Date: Sunday\
 , November 8th\, 2026Time: 10:00am-2:00pm Where: Sebastopol Center for the
  Arts is located at 282 South High Street in Sebastopol\, CA. Details rega
 rding class room and directions will be sent to students 24 hours before t
 he class beings. Price: $67.00 Attendance Price Students: This class is re
 stricted to a maximum of 12 students. Register while you can! If this clas
 s is sold out\, please click where it says ‘sold out’  to join the wai
 tlist! Class Description: In this introductory class\, you will learn basi
 c painting techniques of composition\, value blocking\, and color mixing. 
 Students will be creating a single still life on canvas from start to fini
 sh\, painting objects selected by the instructor. Students will learn to o
 bserve shapes and their relationship to space\, utilize tone and color to 
 demonstrate depth\, light\, and shadow\, and how to complete an acrylic pa
 inting. This class is perfect for beginners\, and painters of all skill-l
 evels\, looking to hone in their acrylic painting skills. This class uses
  donated materials to help support our arts education program and provide 
 cost-friendly\, accessible\, classes! About the Teacher: Ayla Carls is a m
 ultidisciplinary artist in the Bay Area\, with interest in acrylic paintin
 g\, oil pastels\, photography\, print making\, stain glass\, and more! Ayl
 a graduated from the University of SanFrancisco and holds a degree in desi
 gn and fine arts. Ayla has been painting for as long as she can remember\,
  and uses her art practice to connect with herself and her experience in t
 he world around her. Ayla’s practice focuses on capturing the joys aroun
 d us in everyday life\, with the goal of bringing joy to others through ar
 t and creating. Learn more about Ayla on her website here. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n
