BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prescription for Poetry  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Cali
 fornia
DTSTART:20261120T000000
DTEND:20261121T000000
UID:9252883fa1b1d01a7cf3d8613631a5bf@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Prescription for Poetry - November 20th\, 2026\n\n  \n    \n  
     \n        \n          $45.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nFriday\, N
 ovember 20th\, 2026 1:00-5:00pm Fee for this session: $45.00 Prescription 
 for Poetry: A Deeper Dive into Poetic Medicine in Community As a Source of
  HealingSince March 2025\, Redwing Keyssar has been leading monthly Poetic
  Medicine sessions at Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, gathering a vibrant
  community of folks who listen to an write poems together\, as a deeply me
 aningful source of healing\, inspiration and connection. Many people retur
 n each month\, and new folks come and go as well. There has been a yearnin
 g for more time to do this work together in community\, to have time and s
 pace to delve deeper into the thoughts and feelings that emerge and surpri
 se us\, as we hold silence together\, as well as listen deeply and write e
 ffortlessly. And so… we are now offering a seasonal 4-hour Poetic Medici
 ne Session\, beginning on Friday\, November 20th\, from 1:00-5:00pm!What t
 o Bring: your pen/paper/journal/laptop your water bottle your open heart\,
  be ready to be surprised! Some light snacks will be provided. As with the
  monthly sessions: The practice of “poem making” offers a means to exp
 ress the metaphors and meaning of the joys and suffering we experience in 
 ourselves and bear witness to in others. Poetry can be a salve for the hea
 rt and soul. It is a way of speaking what is try in our hearts and is ofte
 n difficult to access without a creative spark. You do not have to be a 
 “poet” or even a “writer” to allow words and feelings to pour thro
 ugh your heart and your pen. About the Instructor: Judith Redwing Keyssar\
 , RN has traversed an amazing 35+ year journey in the healing arts/healthc
 are. Redwing is an educator\, end-of-life doula\, author\, poet\, song-wri
 ter\, ceremonialist\, national presenter and frequent contributor to publi
 c issues about Palliative and End of Life Care. Redwing is currently the D
 irector of Education at the MERI Center for Education in Palliative Care a
 t UCSF/Mt. Zion. Her professional career includes being the Clinical Direc
 tor at Zen Hospice Project and the Director of Palliative Care and Nursing
  at Jewish Family and Children’s Services from 2004-2018. She is a found
 er and adjunct faculty member of the California State University Shiley/Ha
 ynes Institute of Palliative Care\, and has taught courses at OLLI at Sono
 ma State. Redwing is the author of an award-winning book\, “Last Acts of
  Kindness\; Lessons for the Living from the Bedsides of the Dying” and i
 s the recipient of numerous awards in the field of Palliative Care. After 
 studying with John Fox at the Institute for Poetic Medicine\, her passion 
 for using poetry as a healing modality has led to the development of a suc
 cessful international program in Poetic Medicine in Community: Healing Thr
 ough Creativity and Connection\, through her work at the UCSF MERI Center.
  Learn more about her here: https://redwingkeyssar.com/Come find the magic
  in yourself and in the community\, and join us for Prescription for Poetr
 y on Friday\, November 20th\, at 1:00pm.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n
                 Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/prescription-for-poetry
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
